This repository (hymlx) contains an independent MLX reimplementation of the
HunyuanImage-3.0 architecture, written from the published PyTorch reference.
The code here is MIT licensed; see LICENSE.

It does NOT contain any Tencent source code or model weights. At run time it
downloads the official Python modules and the tokenizer from Tencent's
HuggingFace repository into the HuggingFace cache and imports them from there,
so those files reach you under Tencent's own licence.

Any quantised checkpoint produced by tools/convert.py or tools/requantize.py is
a Model Derivative of Tencent Hunyuan and remains subject to the Tencent
Hunyuan Community License Agreement:

    https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/HunyuanImage-3.0/blob/main/LICENSE

Changes made in producing such a checkpoint (as required by Section 3(b) of
that agreement):

  - Weights converted from PyTorch bf16 safetensors to MLX safetensors.
  - Affine group quantisation applied (group size 64). In the released
    checkpoint the 64 routed experts of every layer are quantised to 4 bits and
    all other quantised tensors to 8 bits.
  - Left in bfloat16, unquantised: all normalisation weights, the MoE routing
    gate (mlp.gate.wg), patch_embed, final_layer, time_embed, time_embed_2,
    timestep_emb, the VAE and the SigLIP2 vision tower.
  - The tensor layout was rearranged for MLX (channels-last convolutions;
    the packed gate_and_up_proj split into separate up and gate halves; the
    per-layer experts stacked into a single tensor).
  - No fine-tuning, distillation or other training was performed. Behaviour is
    intended to match the original within quantisation error.

